      "severity": "note",
      "claim": "The spec omits the customary \"Size.\" disclosure that nearly every sibling spec touching saffron/cell/** includes. saffron/cell/session.py and saffron/cell/worktree.py are both under saffron/cell/**, which is in this repo's .saffron/policy.yaml elevate_on list, so effective_risk will compute elevated for this task regardless of the spec not declaring risk: elevated, which makes both the size and witness gates blocking rather than advisory. This is not an actual defect: the stated estimate (1991 changed tokens per the Notes section's measured-prototype figure) sits comfortably under the feature ceiling of 3000, and witness reporting skip for every criterion (since none declares a mutant, as the spec itself notes) is a benign, documented, non-blocking outcome even when witness is the blocking gate. But the omission is a conspicuous gap relative to this repo's own convention, and a person reviewing the spec before the cell starts would reasonably want the elevated-tier fact and the ceiling math spelled out the way every comparable spec does.",
